        /// directory tree and materializes all matches internally before <c>Execute</c> returns, so this method
        /// does not reduce the amount of file-system work compared to <see cref="GlobFiles(ChainablePath, string)"/>.
        /// It is offered for API ergonomics only, e.g. to allow <c>.FirstOrDefault()</c> style chaining without
        /// forcing an intermediate array. Because the sequence is produced lazily on each enumeration, iterating
        /// it more than once will re-run the full underlying directory walk every time.
